[ ] POST /oauth/token          [ ] Accepts client credentials/secret, returns OAuth token.
[ ] GET /users                 [ ] Returns list of users (IDs and usernames).
[ ] GET /users/:id             [ ] Returns target user details (username, avatar, email).
[ ] PATCH /users/:id           [ ] Updates user profile (expects username, email, password, avatar URL).
[ ] GET /movies                [ ] Public endpoint; returns front-page top movie list (IDs and titles).
[ ] GET /movies/:id            [ ] Returns movie metadata, IMDb rating, year, duration, subtitles, comment count.
[ ] GET /comments              [ ] Returns latest comments (author username, date, content, ID).
[ ] GET /comments/:id          [ ] Returns specific comment details.
[ ] POST /comments             [ ] Creates comment (expects comment payload & movie_id).
[ ] PATCH /comments/:id        [ ] Updates comment payload.
[ ] DELETE /comments/:id       [ ] Deletes specific comment.
[x] HTTP ERROR HANDLING        [x] Return appropriate HTTP error status codes for unauthorized/unsupported endpoints.

[x] Additional OAuth2 strategies (e.g., Twitch, Spotify, GitLab).
[x] Multi-resolution video streaming selection (1080p, 720p, 480p).
[ ] Client-side video streaming via MediaStream API.
[x] Extended REST API routes (e.g., admin controls, custom movie management).